<title>DENMARK: Danish Codan Q1 1997 profit rises.</title>
<headline>Danish Codan Q1 1997 profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31 1997</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Group pre-tax result		 189  vs  160</p>
<p> Gross premiums, total		883  vs  871</p>
<p> Life insurance result		 40  vs  49</p>
<p> Result per 100 crown share	  27  vs  34</p>
<p>Own capital end-March 1997  6,123  vs 5,256 end-March 1996</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Denmark's second biggest insurance group is A/S Forsikringsselskabet Codan. The first quarter results were prior to revision.  </p>
<p>Codan said in a statement that the result was satisfactory and added that it maintained its March forecast of a full year 1997 result before securities fluctuations similar to 1996. In 1996 Codan posted a pre-tax profit of 968 million crowns. Codan is 71.45 percent owned by Britain's Dutch-based Royal &amp; Sun Alliance Overseas Holdings BV.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33-969652</p>
